WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.167
U.S.
Central Command says

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:01.901
they're investigating

00:00:01.901 --> 00:00:03.436
an American drone strike in Syria

00:00:03.436 --> 00:00:04.738
that may have resulted in a civilian

00:00:04.738 --> 00:00:05.805
being killed.

00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:06.539
Central Command

00:00:06.539 --> 00:00:08.141
tweeted about the strike afterwards,

00:00:08.141 --> 00:00:09.242
but now there are questions

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:11.044
being raised about what was tweeted

00:00:11.044 --> 00:00:12.078
and why.

00:00:12.078 --> 00:00:13.747
CNN Pentagon correspondent Oren

00:00:13.747 --> 00:00:15.281
Liebermann joins us now with details.

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:16.616
So what do we know

00:00:16.616 --> 00:00:17.684
about the target of the strike

00:00:17.684 --> 00:00:20.353
and what the why sent?

00:00:21.321 --> 00:00:23.790
CENTCOM sent out this tweet.

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:26.292
So the strike was carried out on May 3rd

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:27.660
in northwest Syria,

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.696
targeting a senior al Qaeda leader.

00:00:29.963 --> 00:00:30.930
CENTCOM promised

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:32.132
there would be more information

00:00:32.132 --> 00:00:34.701
when details of the operation itself

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:35.635
were sort of confirmed

00:00:35.635 --> 00:00:36.970
and became available.

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:39.205
But within hours of the strike happening,

00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:40.306
multiple defense officials

00:00:40.306 --> 00:00:42.308
tell CNN that General Eric Khairallah,

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:43.443
the head of U.S.

00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:44.110
Central Command,

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:46.012
ordered the tweet to be put out,

00:00:46.012 --> 00:00:46.946
saying that a senior

00:00:46.946 --> 00:00:48.815
al Qaeda leader had been targeted.

00:00:48.815 --> 00:00:50.450
That is despite high confidence

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:51.451
when the strike itself

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:53.153
was taken that they knew who

00:00:53.153 --> 00:00:54.854
and where they were targeting.

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:55.622
Officials knew

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:56.890
it would still take a few days

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:58.224
to be able to confirm

00:00:58.224 --> 00:00:59.692
who was killed in this strike.

00:00:59.692 --> 00:01:00.593
And that's at least partially

00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:01.795
because there are no U.S.

00:01:01.795 --> 00:01:03.630
troops in northwest Syria,

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:04.130
especially after

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:05.632
the devastating earthquake

00:01:05.632 --> 00:01:07.233
in that part of the country.

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:09.436
And yet this tweet still went out.

00:01:09.436 --> 00:01:11.337
And here we are nearly three weeks later.

00:01:11.337 --> 00:01:12.505
And CENTCOM hasn't put out

00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:14.307
any more information about

00:01:14.307 --> 00:01:15.475
who was the target

00:01:15.475 --> 00:01:17.110
or who was killed in this strike.

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:18.111
Now, CNN has spoken

00:01:18.111 --> 00:01:20.280
to family members of the casualty

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:21.981
who say he was a 56 year

00:01:21.981 --> 00:01:24.150
old farmer who lived in northwest Syria

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:25.151
with ten kids

00:01:25.151 --> 00:01:27.320
and had no affiliation with al Qaeda.

00:01:27.353 --> 00:01:28.254
Anderson,

00:01:28.354 --> 00:01:29.789
So the tweet didn't say

00:01:29.789 --> 00:01:31.724
that they had killed an al Qaeda leader.

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:33.493
It just said that they had targeted one

00:01:33.493 --> 00:01:34.928
and that there would be more information

00:01:34.928 --> 00:01:36.396
and they just never followed up.

00:01:36.396 --> 00:01:37.831
And now locals

00:01:37.831 --> 00:01:38.932
millions are saying that

00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:40.133
a civilian was killed.

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:41.568
Correct.

00:01:41.568 --> 00:01:41.968
So now

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:42.602
there is an

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:43.136
assessment

00:01:43.136 --> 00:01:44.537
on the part of Central Command,

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:45.772
what's known as a C car,

00:01:45.772 --> 00:01:47.607
a civilian casualty

00:01:47.607 --> 00:01:49.142
credibility assessment

00:01:49.142 --> 00:01:50.076
report, which tries

00:01:50.076 --> 00:01:50.910
to figure out

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:52.078
if a civilian was killed,

00:01:52.078 --> 00:01:54.114
if it determines that one was killed.

00:01:54.114 --> 00:01:56.182
That may, depending on the situation,

00:01:56.216 --> 00:01:58.351
the circumstances lead to a more formal

00:01:58.351 --> 00:02:00.186
15 six investigation.

00:02:00.186 --> 00:02:01.488
And that is a more deeper

00:02:01.488 --> 00:02:03.456
look at what went wrong here

00:02:03.456 --> 00:02:05.592
and what was the entire process here.

00:02:05.592 --> 00:02:06.392
Part of the issue

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:08.495
here, Anderson, is the timeline here.

00:02:08.495 --> 00:02:10.697
Strike again was on May 3rd.

00:02:10.697 --> 00:02:11.831
Central Command officials

00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:12.532
and other officials

00:02:12.532 --> 00:02:13.766
tell us that May eight.

00:02:13.766 --> 00:02:15.935
So five days later, The Washington Post

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:17.904
gives information to Central Command

00:02:17.904 --> 00:02:19.038
that suggests

00:02:19.038 --> 00:02:19.973
this may have been a civilian

00:02:19.973 --> 00:02:20.707
casualty killed.

00:02:20.707 --> 00:02:22.342
And it's still another week

00:02:22.342 --> 00:02:24.110
before this assessment is launched.

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:24.811
And we haven't gotten

00:02:24.811 --> 00:02:26.846
to a formal investigation yet.

00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:28.448
So there's a question here of

00:02:28.448 --> 00:02:30.350
why has this taken so long,

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:31.618
especially as some officials

00:02:31.618 --> 00:02:33.386
tell us, the fact that it took so long

00:02:33.386 --> 00:02:34.020
to try to confirm

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:34.754
who was killed here

00:02:34.754 --> 00:02:37.357
in and of itself was a red flag

00:02:37.357 --> 00:02:38.491
So, I mean, obviously,

00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:39.459
look, this is not the first time

00:02:39.459 --> 00:02:40.560
something this has happened.

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:41.828
There was the Kabul strike in 20,

00:02:41.828 --> 00:02:43.530
21 that killed ten civilians

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:44.097
during the U.S.

00:02:44.097 --> 00:02:45.665
withdrawal from Afghanistan.

00:02:45.665 --> 00:02:48.001
Has the Pentagon commented?

00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:49.169
You're exactly right, Anderson.

00:02:49.169 --> 00:02:49.736
And that is

00:02:49.736 --> 00:02:51.871
is very analogous in the closing days

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:53.806
of the withdrawal from Afghanistan.

00:02:53.806 --> 00:02:54.240
A U.S.

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:55.909
drone strike killed ten civilians,

00:02:55.909 --> 00:02:57.377
including seven children.

00:02:57.377 --> 00:02:58.144
The numbers, of course,

00:02:58.144 --> 00:02:58.978
are very different here.

00:02:58.978 --> 00:03:00.213
We're talking about one person

00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:01.748
killed in northwest Syria.

00:03:01.748 --> 00:03:02.882
But again, there

00:03:02.882 --> 00:03:03.816
we saw the military

00:03:03.816 --> 00:03:06.152
initially defending the strike,

00:03:06.152 --> 00:03:06.486
saying

00:03:06.486 --> 00:03:07.987
it was a strike against an ISIS

00:03:07.987 --> 00:03:08.621
key target.

00:03:08.621 --> 00:03:10.023
And they stood by that for weeks

00:03:10.023 --> 00:03:11.491
until the media,

00:03:11.491 --> 00:03:12.292
including CNN,

00:03:12.292 --> 00:03:13.760
reported that this wasn't

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:15.528
any affiliation to ISIS.

00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:17.230
The target of the strike here.

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:18.231
Yet the Pentagon says

00:03:18.231 --> 00:03:19.299
they still have confidence

00:03:19.299 --> 00:03:20.166
in the protocols

00:03:20.166 --> 00:03:21.267
and processes

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:22.869
set up to protect civilians

00:03:22.869 --> 00:03:24.504
in the wake of that strike.

00:03:24.504 --> 00:03:25.905
Here is a brigadier

00:03:25.905 --> 00:03:27.740
General Pat Ryder from earlier today.

00:03:29.842 --> 00:03:32.579
So in terms of CENTCOM's strike,

00:03:33.213 --> 00:03:33.713
as you know,

00:03:33.713 --> 00:03:34.881
they conducted that strike

00:03:34.881 --> 00:03:36.749
on the 3rd of May.

00:03:36.749 --> 00:03:38.585
They are investigating

00:03:38.585 --> 00:03:41.187
the allegations of civilian casualties.

00:03:41.221 --> 00:03:42.455
So, you know,

00:03:42.455 --> 00:03:44.023
I think our record speaks for itself

00:03:44.023 --> 00:03:44.657
in terms of

00:03:44.657 --> 00:03:46.392
how seriously we take these

00:03:46.392 --> 00:03:47.293
very few countries

00:03:47.293 --> 00:03:48.528
around the world do that.

00:03:48.528 --> 00:03:50.230
The secretary has complete confidence

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:51.497
that we will continue to abide

00:03:51.497 --> 00:03:53.933
by the policies that we put into place.

00:03:53.933 --> 00:03:54.934
So the question now,

00:03:54.934 --> 00:03:56.402
how long does this assessment take?

00:03:56.402 --> 00:03:57.904
Does it lead to an investigation?

00:03:57.904 --> 00:03:58.605
And, Anderson,

00:03:58.605 --> 00:03:59.005
at what

00:03:59.005 --> 00:03:59.906
point and will

00:03:59.906 --> 00:04:02.942
there be calls for accountability

00:04:02.942 --> 00:04:04.377
in Libya? And appreciate it. Thank you.

